---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Interval: Spacing Calculator"
  description="A native iPhone utility for evenly spacing repeated objects across a measured span and getting exact mark positions."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-content">
      <span class="section-label">// interval</span>
      <h1>Measure Once.<br />Mark Every Position.</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">
        Interval is a native iPhone utility for evenly spacing repeated objects across a measured span and giving you exact mark positions.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a href="mailto:matt@mattdonders.com?subject=Interval%20Support" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Contact Support</a>
        <a href="/apps/interval/privacy" class="btn btn-outline btn-lg">Privacy Policy</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="section-label">// how it works</span>
        <h2>Get consistent spacing without the guesswork</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="features-grid">
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#128207;</div>
          <h3>Enter the span</h3>
          <p>Start with the total measured distance you need to cover.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#8596;&#65039;</div>
          <h3>Set the repeated objects</h3>
          <p>Choose the number of objects to space across that span.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#128205;</div>
          <h3>Mark exact positions</h3>
          <p>Use the calculated positions to make each mark accurately and evenly.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#128736;&#65039;</div>
          <h3>Built for practical layouts</h3>
          <p>Useful for shelves, hooks, picture spacing, fence posts, trim, and other repeated layouts.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container support-content">
      <span class="section-label">// support</span>
      <h2>Need help with Interval?</h2>
      <p>Send a note and include any details that will help us understand the question.</p>
      <a href="mailto:matt@mattdonders.com?subject=Interval%20Support" class="btn btn-primary">Email Support</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: 6rem 0 5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .hero-content {
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .hero-sub {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    max-width: 52ch;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .btn-lg {
    padding: 0.75rem 1.75rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .features-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .feature-card {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .feature-icon {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .feature-card h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .feature-card p {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .section-alt {
    background: var(--surface);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .support-content {
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .support-content h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .support-content p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .hero { padding: 3rem 0; }
    .features-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
